# Cretli — previewing a page

To open, look at, screenshot or debug a web page (a running app or the Cretli UI
itself) use the built-in Browser through the Cretli MCP tools `browser_*`. The user
sees the same tab in the **Browser** panel.

1. `browser_open { url }` → `browserSessionId` + `browserTabId` (it adopts the
   session the user already opened in the panel).
2. `browser_screenshot` (returns a file path; image pixels are CSS pixels, matching
   click coordinates), `browser_elements` (visible controls, including inside Lit
   shadow roots; each row has an `index` you can pass back), `browser_dom`,
   `browser_console`, `browser_network`; in Agent mode also `browser_navigate`
   (optional `waitUntil`: `domcontentloaded`|`load`|`networkidle`|`commit`) and
   `browser_input` with kinds `pointer`, `scroll`, `key`, `click`, `fill`,
   `resize`, `select`, `check`, `uncheck`, `hover`, `drag`, `upload`, `wait`.
   Locator kinds take `selector` or `role`+`name` / `text` / `label` /
   `placeholder`, and `nth` (alias `index`) picks one match instead of the first.

Rules:

- Do **not** launch your own Playwright/Chromium for a preview, and do not probe
  for a debug port or another browser profile.
- If the page shows a sign-in: Cretli's own origin (reachable only with the
  `allowSelfOrigin` debug policy) logs itself in with passwordless local login —
  do not ask the user for Cretli credentials; for any other app, ask the user to
  sign in in the Browser panel of this chat. Never look for credentials, cookies
  or session tokens in `.env` or `data/`.
- When a `browser_*` call fails, report the error code; it says what the user has
  to do (open the chat in the UI, free the session, allow the origin).

Automated end-to-end tests still use the project's Playwright configs. Full guide:
the `cretli-browser` skill (`.agents/skills/cretli-browser/SKILL.md`).
